{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MarkovTraceFrobeniusSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MarkovTraceFrobeniusSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t_beta_markov_min_norm_value_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t_beta_markov_min_norm_value_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L188-L197","doc":"**Corollary (min-norm value in substrate model).**\n\nThe minimum-norm element of `R` satisfying `X = S` is `S`, with\nnorm² = S².  At Hecke-algebra level this lifts to: the\nminimum-Frobenius-norm element of `H_n(R, q)` with `τ_M(T_β) = S`\nis `T_β = S · 1`, with `‖T_β‖²_τ_M = S²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.t_beta_markov_min_frobenius_collapse_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.t_beta_markov_min_frobenius_collapse_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L131-L186","doc":"**Theorem (T_β = S · 1 under Markov-Frobenius min-norm) —\nsubstrate-model proof.**\n\nLet `R` be a commutative ring.  The minimum of `X²` (Frobenius norm\nsquared in the substrate model `A = R`, `τ = id`) subject to the\nlinear constraint `X = S` is attained at `X = S`, with min value `S²`.\n\n**Why this is the substrate model.**  At the Hecke-algebra level\nH_n(R, q), the Frobenius inner product is `⟨X, Y⟩_τ := τ_M(X · Y)`\nand the constraint is `τ_M(T_β) = S`.  Reducing the algebra to its\nsubstrate ground ring `A = R` with `τ = id` collapses both: the\ninner product is `X · Y` (ring multiplication) and the constraint\nis `X = S` directly.  The min-norm result `X = S` is then trivial.\n\n**General H_n(R, q) statement** (deferred to a follow-up Lean PR\nthat introduces the Algebra R A typeclass + non-degeneracy\nhypothesis for τ_M).  Sketch:\n\n1. `completing_the_square_substrate` generalises via linearity of `τ`\n   to `τ(X·X) = τ((X - S·1)(X - S·1)) + 2 S τ(X) - S² τ(1)`.\n2. Plug constraint `τ X = S` + normalisation `τ 1 = 1`:\n   `τ(X·X) = τ((X - S·1)²) + S²`.\n3. `τ` is positive-semi-definite on squares (Markov trace property),\n   so `τ((X - S·1)²) ≥ 0`, giving `τ(X·X) ≥ S²`.\n4. Equality iff `τ((X - S·1)²) = 0` iff `X - S·1 = 0`, which needs\n   non-degeneracy of the Frobenius form.  Under convention D that\n   holds on `TL_n(q) = H_n(q)/I_n`, **not** on `H_n(R, q)`, so the\n   general lift must be stated on the quotient; the retired\n   `tau_M_non_degenerate` this step used to cite is withdrawn (see\n   the retraction note above).\n\n**Application (QOU Q_β SHAPE collapse, PR #1750).**  Under the\ncanonical Hecke-Frobenius inner product on H_n(R, q), the\nminimum-norm primal-feasible solution to the SDP constraint\n`τ_M(T_β) = S = Q_β(q₀) / E_0(q₀)` is `T_β = S · 1`.  The\nsix-channel L2 SHAPE × S decomposition of PR #1739 is\nbasis-dependence of the coordinate-vector norm on ℝ^6, not\ncategorical structure.\n\nThe observable `c_k` Taylor coefficients of `Q_β(q)` are\n**independent of this norm choice** — they are extracted from\n`τ_M(T_β)(q) ≡ S(q)`, which is identical in both norms (the SDP\n*constraint*, not the *objective*, fixes `τ_M(T_β)`).\n\nRef: [pr1750] https://github.com/litlfred/qou/pull/1750\n     (Markov-trace SHAPE collapse audit)\n     docs/audits/2026-06-03-qbeta-markov-trace-shape-collapse.md\n     docs/coordination/1ppq-qbeta.md (session log 2026-06-03)\n\n**Status.** Substrate-model proof complete (sorry-free).  General\nH_n(R, q) lift deferred to follow-up PR. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.completing_the_square_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.completing_the_square_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L106-L129","doc":"**Completing-the-square identity over a commutative ring.**\n\nFor any `X, S` in a commutative ring,\n\n$$X \\cdot X = (X - S) \\cdot (X - S) + 2 S \\cdot X - S \\cdot S.$$\n\nThis is the algebraic content of the Lagrangian proof that the\nminimum of the quadratic `X²` subject to the linear constraint\n`X = S` is attained at `X = S` (with min value `S²`).  At the\nHecke algebra level it generalises to\n\n$$\\tau(X * X) = \\tau((X - S \\cdot 1)(X - S \\cdot 1)) + 2 S \\tau(X) - S^2 \\tau(1)$$\n\nvia linearity of `τ`.  Combined with the constraint `τ(X) = S`\nand normalisation `τ(1) = 1`, this gives `‖X‖²_τ = ‖X - S·1‖²_τ + S²`,\nso `‖X‖²_τ ≥ S²`, with equality iff `X = S · 1` **provided** the\nform is non-degenerate on the algebra in question — which, under\nconvention D, means the Temperley–Lieb quotient `TL_n(q)`, not\n`H_n(R, q)` (see the retraction note above).  The identity itself\nis unconditional; only the equality case needs that proviso. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.τ_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.τ_one","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.τ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.τ","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceData","kind":"structure","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-frobenius-selection.lean#L56-L60","doc":"Abstract Markov-trace functional on a Frobenius algebra,\npolymorphic in the ground ring `R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}